== Source roles ==

* SEP Turing Machines / Computability and Complexity — theoretical computation.
* OpenDSA — formal languages, automata, Turing machines and language hierarchy.
* ACM CS2023 — current curricular boundaries for architecture, OS, databases, networking and human factors.
* NIST CSRC / DADS — security, cryptography and state-machine terminology.
* standard architecture/OS/network/database/compiler/distributed-systems texts — systems foundations.
* HCI texts and ACM literature — interaction and human factors.
* Singer & Draper (SPLASH 2025), Temkin and related academic work — esoteric programming languages.

